+</span><br/><span id="fn194"><a href="#r194">194</a>&nbsp;This extract discloses to us (in connexion with the passages from Dionysius Alex. here and in the de Sent. D. ) a remarkable anticipation of the Arian controversy in the third century. 1. It appears that the very symbol of hn ote ouk hn ec ouk ontwn adiaireton, anarxon, aeigenej
+</span><br/><span id="fn195"><a href="#r195">195</a>&nbsp;filoponou
