+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn118' href="#_ednref118"
+name="_edn118" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>18 </sup>Isa.
+lxiii. 9 (LXX.), and the note in the (Queen&#8217;s Printers&#8217;) &#8216;Variorum&#8217; Bible.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn119>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn119' href="#_ednref119"
+name="_edn119" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>19 </sup>Athan.
+here assumes, for the purpose of his argument, the principles of the
+Neo-platonist schools. They were influenced, in regard to the Logos, by Philo,
+but even on this subject the germ of their teaching may be traced in Plato,
+especially in the <i>Timoeus,</i> (See Drummond&#8217;s <i>Philo,</i> i. 65&#8211;88.
+Bigg&#8217;s <i>Bamp. Lect.</i> 14, 18, 248&#8211;253, and St. Aug. <i>Confess.</i> in
+&#8216;Nicene Fathers,&#8217; Series 1, vol. 1, p. 107 and notes.)</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn120>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn120' href="#_ednref120"
+name="_edn120" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>20 </sup>Especially
+Plato, <i>Tim.</i> 30, &amp;c.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn121>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn121' href="#_ednref121"
+name="_edn121" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>21 </sup><span
+lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:EL'>epibebhkenai</span>,
+cf. above, 20. 4, 6. The Union of God and Man in Christ is of course
+&#8216;hypostatic&#8217; or personal, and thus (<i>supra</i> 17. 1), different in kind from
+the union of the Word with Creation. His argument is <i>ad homines.</i> It was
+not for thinkers who identified the Universe with God to take exception to the
+idea of Incarnation. </p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn122>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn122' href="#_ednref122"
+name="_edn122" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>22 </sup>See
+Acts. xvii. 28.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn123>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn123' href="#_ednref123"
+name="_edn123" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>23 </sup><span
+lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:EL'>epibainwn</span>, see
+supra, note 3.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn124>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn124' href="#_ednref124"
+name="_edn124" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>24 </sup>The
+superfluous <span lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:EL'>pepoihkenai</span>
+is ignored, being untranslateable as the text stands. For a less simple
+conjecture, see the Bened. note.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn125>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:
+none;text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn125' href="#_ednref125"
+name="_edn125" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>25 </sup>This
+thought is beautifully expressed by Keble :&#8212;</p>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.25in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-pagination:
+none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:
+11.0pt'>&#8216;All true, all faultless, all in tune, Creation&#8217;s wondrous choir</span></p>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.25in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-pagination:
+none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:
+11.0pt'>Opened in mystic unison, to last till time expire.<o:p/></span></p>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.25in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-pagination:
+none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:
+11.0pt'>And still it lasts: by day and night with one consenting voice<o:p/></span></p>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.25in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-pagination:
+none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:
+11.0pt'>All hymn Thy glory Lord, aright, all worship and rejoice:<o:p/></span></p>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.25in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-pagination:
+none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:
+11.0pt'>Man only mars the sweet accord&#8221; &#8230;.<o:p/></span></p>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:11.0pt'>(&#8216;Christian Year,&#8217; Fourth
+Sunday after Trinity.) <o:p/></span></p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn126>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn126' href="#_ednref126"
+name="_edn126" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>26 </sup>Cf.
+41. 5, note 3.<span style='font-size:11.0pt'><o:p/></span></p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn127>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn127' href="#_ednref127"
+name="_edn127" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>27 </sup>Cf.
+Orig. <i>c. Cels.</i> vi. 64, where there is the same contrast between <span
+lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:EL'>metecein</span> and <span
+lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:EL'>metecesqai</span>.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn128>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn128' href="#_ednref128"
+name="_edn128" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>28 </sup>Ath.
+paraphrases loosely Plat. <i>Politic.</i> 273 D. See Jowett&#8217;s Plato (ed. 2)
+vol. iv. pp. 515, 553.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn129>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn129' href="#_ednref129"
+name="_edn129" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>29 </sup>Lit.
+&#8220;sate down&#8221;, as four lines above.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn130>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn130' href="#_ednref130"
+name="_edn130" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>30 </sup>With
+this discussion compare that upon &#8216;repentance&#8217; above 7. (esp. 7. 4).</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn131>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn131' href="#_ednref131"
+name="_edn131" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>31 </sup>Restoration
+by a mere fiat would have shewn God&#8217;s <i>power,</i> the Incarnation shews His <i>Love.</i>
+See Orat. i. 52, note 1, ii. 68, note 1.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn132>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn132' href="#_ednref132"
+name="_edn132" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>32 </sup>Cf.
+<i>Orat.</i> i. 56, note 5, 65, note 3. </p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn133>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn133' href="#_ednref133"
+name="_edn133" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>33 </sup>See
+above 28. 3. He appears not to have seen the substance.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn134>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn134' href="#_ednref134"
+name="_edn134" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>34 </sup>Isa.
+xi. 9. For the arguments, compare &sect;&sect;11&#8211;14.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn135>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn135' href="#_ednref135"
+name="_edn135" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>35 </sup>See
+D&ouml;llinger, <i>Gentile and Jew,</i> i. 449.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn136>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn136' href="#_ednref136"
+name="_edn136" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>36 </sup>Col.
+ii. 15.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn137>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn137' href="#_ednref137"
+name="_edn137" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>37 </sup>The
+Incarnation completes the circle of God&#8217;s self-witness and of man&#8217;s
+responsibility.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn138>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn138' href="#_ednref138"
+name="_edn138" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>38 </sup>Cf.
+notes on <i>c. Gent.</i> 10, and 12. 2.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn139>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn139' href="#_ednref139"
+name="_edn139" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>39 </sup>On
+the following argument see D&ouml;llinger ii. 210 <i>sqq.</i>, and Bigg, <i>Bampt.
+Lect.</i> 248, note 1. </p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn140>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn140' href="#_ednref140"
+name="_edn140" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>40 </sup>On
+the local character of ancient religions, see D&ouml;llinger i. 109, &amp;c., and
+Coulanges, <i>La Cit&eacute; Antique,</i> Book III. ch. vi., and V. iii. (the
+substance in Barker&#8217;s <i>Aryan Civilisation</i>).</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn141>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn141' href="#_ednref141"
+name="_edn141" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>41 </sup>On
+these, see D&ouml;llinger, i. 216, &amp;c., and Milton&#8217;s <i>Ode on the Nativity,</i>
+stanza xix.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn142>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn142' href="#_ednref142"
+name="_edn142" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>42 </sup>i.e.
+that of Trophonius.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn143>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn143' href="#_ednref143"
+name="_edn143" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>43 </sup>Patara.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn144>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn144' href="#_ednref144"
+name="_edn144" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>44 </sup>Ammon.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn145>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn145' href="#_ednref145"
+name="_edn145" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>45 </sup>See
+D&ouml;llinger, i. 73, 164&#8211;70: the Cabiri were pre-Hellenic deities, worshipped in
+many ancient sanctuaries, but principally in Samothrace and Lemnos.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn146>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn146' href="#_ednref146"
+name="_edn146" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>46 </sup>Cf.
+<i>Vit. Ant.</i> xvi.-xliii., also D&ouml;llinger, ii. 212, and a curious catena of
+extracts from early Fathers, collected by Hurter in &#8216;Opuscula SS. Patrum
+Selecta,&#8217; vol 1, appendix.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn147>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn147' href="#_ednref147"
+name="_edn147" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>47 </sup>For
+this opinion, see note 1 on <i>c. Gent.</i> 12.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn148>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn148' href="#_ednref148"
+name="_edn148" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>48 </sup>See
+D&ouml;llinger, ii. 210, and (on Julian) 215.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn149>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn149' href="#_ednref149"
+name="_edn149" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>49 </sup>In
+Plato&#8217;s ideal Republic, the notion of any direct influence of the highest
+ideals upon the masses is quite absent. Their happiness is to be in passive
+obedience to the few whom those ideals inspire. (Contrast Isa. liv. 13, Jer.
+xxxi. 34.)</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn150>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn150' href="#_ednref150"
+name="_edn150" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>50 </sup>Cf.
+<i>Hist. Arian.</i> 25, <i>Apol. Const.</i> 33. </p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn151>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn151' href="#_ednref151"
+name="_edn151" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>51 </sup><i>e.g.</i>
+Iamblichus, &amp;c., cf. Introd. to <i>c. Gent.</i></p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn152>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn152' href="#_ednref152"
+name="_edn152" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>52 </sup>Cf.
+Thucy. i. 5 6: &#8216;<span lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:
+EL'>pasa gar h {Ella&quot; esidhroforei,</span>&#8217; &amp;c.<i><o:p/></i></p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn153>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn153' href="#_ednref153"
+name="_edn153" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>53 </sup>Isa.
+ii. 4. </p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn154>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn154' href="#_ednref154"
+name="_edn154" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>54 </sup>St.
+Augustine, Civ. D. IV. xvi. commenting on the fact that the temple of &#8216;Repose&#8217;
+(Quies) at Rome was not within the city walls, suggests &#8216;qui illam turbam
+colere perseveraret &#8230;doemoniorum, cure Quietem hahere non posse.&#8217;</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn155>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn155' href="#_ednref155"
+name="_edn155" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>55 </sup>1
+Cor. ii. 8.</p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn156>
+
+<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;
+text-autospace:none'><a style='mso-endnote-id:edn156' href="#_ednref156"
+name="_edn156" title=""><span class=MsoEndnoteReference>1</span></a><sup>56 </sup><span
+lang=EL style='font-family:GraecaII;mso-ansi-language:EL'>qeopoihqwmen</span>.
+See <i>Orat.</i> ii. 70, note 1, and many other passages in those Discourses,
+as well as <i>Letters</i> 60. 4, 61 2. (Eucharistic reference), <i>de Synodis</i>
+51, note 7. (Compare also Iren. IV. xxxviii. 4, &#8216;non ab initio dii facti sumus,
+sed primo quidem homines, tunc demum dii,&#8217; cf. <i>ib.</i> praef. 4. <i>fin.</i>
+also V. ix. 2, &#8216;sublevat in vitam Dei.&#8217; Origen <i>Cels.</i> iii. 28 <i>fin.</i>
+touches the same thought, but Ath. is here in closer affinity to the idea of
+Irenaeus than to that of Origen.) The New Test. reference is 2 Pet. i. 4,
+rather than Heb. ii. 9 sqq; the Old Test., Ps. lxxxii. 6, which seems to
+underlie Orat. iii. 25 (note 5). In spite of the last mentioned passage, &#8216;God&#8217;
+is far preferable as a rendering, in most places, to &#8216;gods,&#8217; which has
+heathenish associations. To us (1 Cor. viii. 6) there are no such things as
+&#8216;gods.&#8217; (The best summary of patristic teaching on this subject is given by
+Harnack <i>Dg.</i> ii. p. 46 note.) </p>
+
+</div>
+
+<div style='mso-element:endnote' id=edn157>
+
