+Swear to me by the body and blood of our Lord Jesus Christ that you will never forsake me and turn to Cornelius.'<br/><br/>
+19 And the unhappy man does not taste until he has called down imprecations on himself; and instead of saying Amen, as he takes the bread, he says, I will never return to Cornelius." Farther on he says again:<br/><br/>
+20 "But know that he has now been made bare and desolate; as the brethren leave him every day and return to the church. Moses<sup><a href="#fn369" id="r369">369</a></sup> also, the blessed martyr, who lately suffered among us a glorious and admirable martyrdom, while he was yet alive, beholding his boldness and folly, refused to commune with him and with the five presbyters who with him had separated themselves from the church."<br/><br/>
